WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.919
There are several asian languages that
are commonly studied around the world

00:00:03.919 --> 00:00:08.639
like mandarin japanese and korean one
asian language that's less commonly

00:00:08.639 --> 00:00:11.280
studied but is still an important major
language

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.679
is vietnamese or as it's called in
vietnamese

00:00:15.679 --> 00:00:20.880
vietnamese is the first language of
around 85 to 90 million people worldwide

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:25.119
most of them in vietnam of course while
several million vietnamese people abroad

00:00:25.119 --> 00:00:28.480
also speak it
it's also the second language of 10 to

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:32.320
15 percent of vietnam's population
since there are many linguistic

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:36.600
minorities in vietnam vietnamese is part
of the mon khmer branch of the

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:41.040
austroasiatic language family
it's by far the austroasiatic language

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:44.960
with the most speakers
the second most spoken being khmer or

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:47.840
kamae
as they call it the base of vietnamese

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:51.039
is mon khmer
but similar to japanese and korean

00:00:51.039 --> 00:00:55.120
vietnamese has undergone a tremendous
amount of influence from chinese

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:59.280
vietnam came under almost continuous
chinese rule for a period of around a

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:02.960
thousand years
beginning in the year 111 bce around

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:06.479
this time or earlier
proto-viet mong the ancestor of the

00:01:06.479 --> 00:01:10.240
vietnamese and
wong languages arose as we'll see later

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:14.479
vietnamese is a tonal language
but proto-viet wong did not yet contain

00:01:14.479 --> 00:01:17.439
any tones
it might be tempting to conclude that

00:01:17.439 --> 00:01:21.360
vietnamese adopted its tones from
chinese but that's very unlikely

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:25.280
both the tones of chinese and the tones
of vietnamese arose naturally through a

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:28.640
process of
tonogenesis meaning that the tones arose

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:33.119
from other phonological features
as the proto-vietnamese language arose

00:01:33.119 --> 00:01:36.240
from proto-vietng
it first developed three-tone

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:40.159
distinctions after this
by the 9th century a huge amount of

00:01:40.159 --> 00:01:42.880
chinese vocabulary began to enter the
language

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:46.000
because the formal written language was
classical chinese

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.439
with characteristic vietnamese
pronunciation and attempts to write

00:01:49.439 --> 00:01:52.880
vernacular vietnamese were made using
chinese characters

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:56.960
today approximately thirty percent of
commonly used words are of chinese

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:59.680
origin
while in formal texts that rises to

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:03.759
sixty percent or even seventy percent
for example this recent newspaper

00:02:03.759 --> 00:02:08.399
headline meaning the price of jackfruit
drops to the floor farmers suffer heavy

00:02:08.399 --> 00:02:11.440
losses
in this example 4 out of 8 words are of

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:14.640
chinese origin
the system of writing using entirely

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:20.480
chinese characters was called
or then after vietnam returned to

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:24.000
vietnamese rule
under the ngo dynasty a new system was

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:28.000
developed in which chinese characters
were used for words of chinese origin

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:31.920
and some native vietnamese words while
newly created characters were used for

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:36.400
vietnamese words
this system was called

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:40.319
the new characters were adaptations or
combinations of existing chinese

00:02:40.319 --> 00:02:43.840
characters or their elements
but they weren't used in chinese we can

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:47.519
see an example of this in the name of
this writing system

00:02:47.519 --> 00:02:52.000
the second character exists in chinese
but the first one doesn't

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:56.000
from the 15th century to the 19th
century this system was used for writing

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:00.400
vietnamese literature such as
the tale of qiu perhaps the most famous

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:04.400
vietnamese work of poetry
also by the start of this period the

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:07.680
three tones of vietnamese had split into
its present six

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:11.519
tones meanwhile classical chinese
continued to be used for official

00:03:11.519 --> 00:03:15.120
writing and amongst the elite
this situation continued until the

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:19.040
french occupation of vietnam which began
in the 19th century

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:22.720
french replaced chinese as the language
of administration and the elite

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:26.959
and the french encouraged the use of to
write vietnamese

00:03:26.959 --> 00:03:30.720
the name of the script means national
language script and is the current

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:34.000
writing system which is based on a
modified latin alphabet

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:38.000
it was first created by portuguese
missionaries in the 17th century but

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:41.120
didn't become widespread until the
french were in power

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:45.280
french influence on vietnamese also took
place in the form of loanwords

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:48.799
even though they may not stand out as
french because of their vietnamese

00:03:48.799 --> 00:03:53.840
pronunciation and spelling
for example coffee cafe in french

00:03:53.840 --> 00:04:01.599
meaning coffee in the word
from meaning railway station

00:04:01.599 --> 00:04:08.560
from fromage meaning cheese so me
in the word comes from

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:14.640
meaning shirt from
meaning soap as you can see a lot of the

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:17.040
french loanwords are common everyday
words

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:20.320
but there are far fewer of them than
there are chinese loanwords

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:24.320
one study concluded that ninety percent
of loanwords come from chinese while

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:28.240
four percent come from french
if you found the pronunciation of those

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:32.080
french loanwords disorienting then
you've just experienced a touch of what

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:34.880
most learners find challenging about
vietnamese

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:38.880
it's phonology while vietnamese is quite
straightforward in other ways

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:43.759
its phonology is fairly complex standard
vietnamese doesn't officially have

00:04:43.759 --> 00:04:47.520
standardized pronunciation
the hanoi dialect is sometimes thought

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:51.199
of as a de facto standard
and is the variety used in most of this

00:04:51.199 --> 00:04:54.880
video but there are many varieties with
different pronunciation

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:58.880
including the dialect of ho chi minh
which is obviously an important one

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:01.919
northern vietnamese basically has 19
consonants

00:05:01.919 --> 00:05:05.360
while there are 23 consonants if we
include all dialects

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:09.680
they're written with 16 single consonant
letters 10 consonant digraphs

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:14.560
and one consonant trigraph that's a
total of 27 consonant graphemes

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:18.639
meaning that some consonant sounds are
written in more than one way

00:05:18.639 --> 00:05:22.160
there are 11 vowel sounds written with
12 graphemes

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:27.840
as well as 28 or more diphthongs and 12
or more triphthongs

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:31.280
standard vietnamese also has six
phonemic tones

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:34.400
meaning that different tones indicate a
difference in meaning

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:42.080
the tones are flat mid ma low falling
ma high rising ma low falling broken

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:46.240
ma low falling rising ma high rising
broken

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:50.240
ma notice that each of these syllables
is a different word with a different

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:54.000
meaning
for example ma means the ghost while

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:59.600
ma means mom when you include all the
different phonemes including tones there

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:04.000
are between 4
500 and 4 800 possible syllables in

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:06.479
spoken vietnamese depending on the
dialect

00:06:06.479 --> 00:06:11.039
and vietnamese orthography can represent
6200 different syllables

00:06:11.039 --> 00:06:15.840
any syllable that appears in any dialect
several learners of vietnamese whom i've

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:18.400
spoken to
told me that learning to produce all the

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:22.080
different phonemes of vietnamese
is really just a matter of practice but

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:25.759
that building listening comprehension
skills is the bigger challenge

00:06:25.759 --> 00:06:28.960
but not everything about vietnamese is
difficult or complicated

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:33.280
its grammar is fairly straightforward
vietnamese is an analytic language

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:37.039
meaning that there are no inflections
and grammatical relationships between

00:06:37.039 --> 00:06:40.240
words are shown through word order and
by adding adjacent

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:44.240
helper words instead this means that you
don't have to learn various forms of

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:46.479
words
there are no case inflections no

00:06:46.479 --> 00:06:50.080
conjugations no grammatical genders and
no plural form

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:54.880
you just learn one form of each word
people sometimes refer to vietnamese as

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:58.400
a monosyllabic language but that's not
precisely accurate

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:02.080
many words have two syllables especially
compound words that consist

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:06.080
of two independent words put together
but if you separate those two pieces of

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:09.440
the word each of those pieces
is normally a meaningful independent

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:13.520
word on its own those words that join
together to form compound words don't

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:16.479
always have one syllable each but they
usually do

00:07:16.479 --> 00:07:20.319
also it's worth noting that more
compound words are used in writing and

00:07:20.319 --> 00:07:23.039
formal speech
so there are a lot more monosyllabic

00:07:23.039 --> 00:07:27.039
words in colloquial speech
the basic word order of vietnamese is

00:07:27.039 --> 00:07:30.160
svo
for example the sentence meaning he ate

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:34.319
dinner
here's the subject here's the verb and

00:07:34.319 --> 00:07:38.240
here's the object
adverbs usually come after verbs and

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:41.919
after the object of the verb if there is
one

00:07:41.919 --> 00:07:46.240
this means he ate dinner early
adjectives also come after the nouns

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:48.639
they modify
like this phrase meaning the nice

00:07:48.639 --> 00:07:53.280
restaurant
literally restaurant beautiful so do

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:58.400
demonstrative adjectives
that restaurant literally restaurant

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:01.199
that
possessives come after nouns as well

00:08:01.199 --> 00:08:06.879
sometimes with a possession marker
his restaurant literally restaurant

00:08:06.879 --> 00:08:10.240
possession marker
he the possession marker is sometimes

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:13.120
dropped when talking about subjects such
as parents

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:16.479
home or school but in this case it's
necessary

00:08:16.479 --> 00:08:20.479
in equational sentences there's no verb
meaning to be when the predicate is an

00:08:20.479 --> 00:08:24.400
adjective
this means hong is smart but when the

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:30.400
predicate is a noun or a noun
phrase then the linking verb la is used

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:33.760
hong is a singer word for word the
sentence is hong

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:38.719
is singer note that vietnamese does not
have articles so this sentence has no

00:08:38.719 --> 00:08:43.519
equivalent of the word ah
the cardinal number is sometimes used in

00:08:43.519 --> 00:08:45.440
a way
similar to the english indefinite

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:50.959
article in this case it might be used to
emphasize indefiniteness

00:08:50.959 --> 00:08:56.000
this too means hong is a singer verbs in
vietnamese always have the same form

00:08:56.000 --> 00:09:00.160
there are no conjugations tense and
aspect is expressed with time markers

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:06.880
that come before the verb
this means he rides a motorbike

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:09.839
he rode a motorbike

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:13.279
he's riding a motorbike

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:18.480
tomorrow he will ride a motorbike there
are also some adverbs that can be used

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:20.880
to show the action's relationship to
time

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:25.839
sometimes alone and sometimes together
with a time marker

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:30.640
he's about to come here tomorrow to
borrow my motorbike word for word it's

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:36.880
he about to come here to borrow
motorbike of me the main thing to note

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:39.200
here is that the verb itself never
changes

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:42.480
another word is added to give
information about time

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:45.920
let's go back to the present tense
sentence and add something i'm going to

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:49.920
lie more just in my model
this means he rides a red motorbike word

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:54.080
for word it's
he ride one counter motorbike color

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:58.560
red this word here is a classifier or a
counter

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:02.560
like a unit for counting nouns that
differs depending on the category of

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:04.880
noun
in english there's some limited use of

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:09.440
words like this like a pair of pants or
sheets of paper but in vietnamese

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:12.720
they're much more frequently used
they come after the number and before

00:10:12.720 --> 00:10:17.200
the noun this one's used for vehicles
and for individual items in a set of

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:20.800
items
these are the most common counters this

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:25.360
is a counter for people
for example meaning two americans

00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:30.800
there's a different classifier for other
animate nouns which are normally animals

00:10:30.800 --> 00:10:34.720
i have a dog for inanimate nouns there
are lots of different specific

00:10:34.720 --> 00:10:38.800
classifiers but there's one very common
one that can be used for most inanimate

00:10:38.800 --> 00:10:41.680
objects in general

00:10:42.560 --> 00:10:46.720
he bought two pens note that in each of
these cases the counter comes after the

00:10:46.720 --> 00:10:50.880
cardinal number and before the noun
now let's look at a couple of questions

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:53.200
and possible answers and see what we
find

00:10:53.200 --> 00:10:57.040
this question means do you drink alcohol
not go on zero

00:10:57.040 --> 00:11:00.399
word for word it's you confirmation
particle drink

00:11:00.399 --> 00:11:04.959
alcohol negation marker yes or no
questions are commonly formed using the

00:11:04.959 --> 00:11:09.120
words
which are also used to answer such a

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:14.240
question with yes or no
comes after the subject and comes at the

00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:16.560
end
it's kind of like saying you do drink

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:21.040
alcohol no
um no i don't drink alcohol

00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:26.399
word for word no i no drink alcohol
notice here that the negation marker

00:11:26.399 --> 00:11:32.160
comes before the verb
yes i drink alcohol word for word it's

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:36.320
confirmation particle
i drink alcohol there's the confirmation

00:11:36.320 --> 00:11:39.839
particle the same one that appears in
the question

00:11:39.839 --> 00:11:43.440
another question this time an open
question man somewhere though

00:11:43.440 --> 00:11:51.360
word for word it's you live in where
i live in hanoi i live in hanoi

00:11:51.360 --> 00:11:55.519
open questions are basically formed by
substituting the question word for the

00:11:55.519 --> 00:11:58.079
word that
answers the question some question words

00:11:58.079 --> 00:12:01.600
come at the beginning of the sentence
and some come at the end

00:12:01.600 --> 00:12:04.720
it's worth mentioning something about
the personal pronouns these are

00:12:04.720 --> 00:12:08.560
basically neutral polite pronouns but
there are actually numerous different

00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:11.279
pronouns to choose from depending on the
gender and

00:12:11.279 --> 00:12:15.040
age or social position of the person
you're speaking to this is another one

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:17.360
of the challenging things for learners
of vietnamese

00:12:17.360 --> 00:12:21.279
on the easier side personal pronouns
remain the same regardless of whether

00:12:21.279 --> 00:12:25.760
they're a subject or an object
the examples so far have been in

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:29.760
northern vietnamese but vietnamese has
three main dialect groups

00:12:29.760 --> 00:12:33.279
northern in particular hanoi central and
southern

00:12:33.279 --> 00:12:37.600
in particular the ho chi minh dialect
naturally the northern dialect of hanoi

00:12:37.600 --> 00:12:41.519
and the southern dialect of ho chi minh
are both popular for learners and of

00:12:41.519 --> 00:12:45.200
course there are differences
northern vietnamese has six tones as we

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:48.560
saw before
while southern vietnamese has five two

00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:51.839
of the tones represented in writing are
pronounced the same in southern

00:12:51.839 --> 00:12:55.920
vietnamese
so in northern vietnamese there's ma and

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:58.610
ma in southern vietnamese there's

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:05.040
also the general range of pitches used
is higher in the north and lower in the

00:13:05.040 --> 00:13:07.360
south
even though the relative contours of the

00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:10.880
pitches are similar
another difference is that the letter d

00:13:10.880 --> 00:13:15.440
and the digraph gi
are pronounced z in the north but ye in

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:18.560
the south
for example this word meaning easy in

00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:23.760
northern vietnamese
and in southern vietnamese another

00:13:23.760 --> 00:13:27.680
letter that's pronounced as
za in northern vietnamese is r in

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:31.600
southern vietnamese it's pronounced
similar to the r sound commonly used in

00:13:31.600 --> 00:13:35.200
english
for example the word for alcohol in

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:39.760
northern vietnamese
and in southern vietnamese another

00:13:39.760 --> 00:13:43.360
difference lies in the letter
v which is pronounced in northern

00:13:43.360 --> 00:13:46.399
vietnamese but in southern vietnamese
it's

00:13:46.399 --> 00:13:50.079
at least in casual conversation for
example the word for ticket

00:13:50.079 --> 00:13:53.839
in northern vietnamese and in southern
vietnamese

00:13:53.839 --> 00:13:59.680
yeah also s and x are both pronounced
si in hanoi and much of the north but in

00:13:59.680 --> 00:14:02.880
southern vietnamese
s

00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:07.920
for example the word for excellent in
northern vietnamese

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:13.040
and in southern vietnamese another
difference is that the digraphs tr

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:19.839
and ch are both pronounced in the north
in the south tr is pronounced and ch is

00:14:19.839 --> 00:14:22.639
pronounced
but these days more people pronounce

00:14:22.639 --> 00:14:25.920
them the same
there's also a significant number of

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:28.079
different words between the two
varieties

00:14:28.079 --> 00:14:32.560
we can see one example in this sentence
from before

00:14:32.560 --> 00:14:36.240
and here it is in southern vietnamese

00:14:36.720 --> 00:14:40.959
notice the different word for pen this
is just one example but there are

00:14:40.959 --> 00:14:45.680
numerous different words like this
as you can see vietnamese is a very

00:14:45.680 --> 00:14:48.720
interesting language
it may not be the easiest language for

00:14:48.720 --> 00:14:52.079
learners to take on and its phonology
may present a challenge

00:14:52.079 --> 00:14:55.440
but in certain ways it's a very
straightforward language if you've ever

00:14:55.440 --> 00:14:58.320
been
frustrated by cases in german or verb

00:14:58.320 --> 00:15:01.600
conjugations in spanish
then vietnamese grammar might be a

00:15:01.600 --> 00:15:04.399
breath of fresh air
and most learners say it's a fun

00:15:04.399 --> 00:15:08.560
language to learn especially if you have
a growth mindset and a long-term view

00:15:08.560 --> 00:15:11.839
for the language
the question of the day for speakers of

00:15:11.839 --> 00:15:15.600
vietnamese how easy is it for you to
communicate with speakers of other

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:18.079
dialects
and for other people what's your

00:15:18.079 --> 00:15:21.360
impression of vietnamese
what seems challenging and what seems

00:15:21.360 --> 00:15:25.440
straightforward this is the part of the
video when i say thanks to the langfocus

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:29.199
patreon supporters especially these ones
right here on the screen because they

00:15:29.199 --> 00:15:31.920
are
the top tier patreon supporters so many

00:15:31.920 --> 00:15:36.320
extra special thanks go out to them
and to everyone thank you for watching

00:15:36.320 --> 00:15:41.839
and have a nice
day

00:15:58.160 --> 00:16:00.240
you

